[h1]The Wall — CWYS[/h1]

A mountainous continent stands between the Old World and the lands farther west. Its almost entirely impassable spine makes the Wall a serious obstacle: reaching its coast is only the first step. The way through is to land at the narrow, passable stretch and establish a foothold there.

Explore from the Old World or start as a native country in a world already home to hundreds of states and tribes.

[h2]🌎 What awaits you[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]A real barrier to the west:[/b] A long north–south continent with deeply indented shores and a mountain spine that leaves very little room to cross. Choosing where to land is central to pushing beyond the Wall.
[*][b]Land beyond the mountains:[/b] Further continents and islands lie to the west, spread across the expanded Pacific. Getting through the Wall opens the way to a much larger New World.
[*][b]An inhabited New World:[/b] 399 native states and 505 tribes, with their own cultures, religions and relationships. You can lead one of them or encounter them as an overseas power.
[*][b]Established regional powers:[/b] Four great empires, three sacred centres, a fractured realm and a maritime league give the world several different political centres.
[*][b]Rivers, lakes and varied terrain:[/b] The generated lands contain 7,101 land locations and 201 lakes, with climates, river systems and sea routes shaped around the new geography.
[*][b]Resources worth seeking:[/b] Gold, silver and gem deposits, along with pearl-producing coasts, give explorers and native powers valuable places to compete over.
[/list]

The Old World remains unchanged.

[h2]▶ How to play[/h2]
This download contains a complete, ready-to-play world. Subscribe, enable this map in your playset and start a new 1337 campaign. You do not need to run or enable the RNW generator to play it.

Use one RNW world at a time. Restart EU5 when switching maps, and keep this world mod for its saves.

Generator compatibility: EU5 1.4.*. New patches in this branch are usually compatible without waiting for a generator update; latest fully verified: 1.4.7. This ready-made map was generated with RNW 1.1.0 on EU5 1.4.6, so continue its campaigns on that exact game version. Across the Pillars is optional.

